ing|chopped]]\n* 2 branches [[Cookbook:Lemongrass|lemongrass]], smashed\n* 3 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], pressed\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Scallion|scallions]], chopped\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Grater|grated]] [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger root]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]] seed\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Caraway|caraway]] seed\n* 4 whole [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Terasi|trassi]]\n* 3 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Oil and Fat|oil]]\n==Procedure==\n#Grind the green chilli peppers, garlic, lemongrass, and scallions in a [[Cookbook:Mortar and Pestle|mortar]].\n#Add the remaining ingredients except for the oil, and keep grinding to a fluid paste.\n#Mix in the oil.\n#Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 1 month.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Alternatively, instead of using a mortar and pestle, you can add all ingredients to a [[Cookbook:Food Processor|food processor]] or [[Cookbook:Blender|blender]] and process until smooth. Thin with water or oil as necessary.\n\n[[Category:Thai recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for curry]]\n[[Category:Recipes using caraway]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using nutmeg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemongrass]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Thai Green Curry Paste","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"16 green piri-piri chilli-peppers, chopped","sourceText":"16 green piri-piri chilli-peppers, chopped","amountText":"16 green piri-piri chilli-peppers, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 branches lemongrass, smashed","sourceText":"2 branches lemongrass, smashed","amountText":"2 branches lemongrass, smashed","amount":nul